                <pb facs="0963" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/223: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-05T11:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 5—10:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Following from Vladivostok dated April 4, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>“The Japanese publicity bureau states that Chita government forces numbering
                    about 800 attacked the Japanese with (?) quite near Spassk Sunday as reply to
                    the request to leave neutral territory. Chita casualties 80, Japanese none.
                    There were several minor collisions yesterday and according to same source four
                    Japanese aeroplanes bombarded Chita government positions at three stations
                    including Sviyagino.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
